text Her previously high tension is nowhere to be seen now.
text We just sit here, gazing at the tiny fire.
text Maybe we shouldn't have lit it up at all.
text The silence is making the fire look as if it's mourning.
text Flickering slowly as if remembering something...
text So fragile is its existence...
text The classroom is flickering along with the fire...
text Even the flow of time... everything is inside a fleeting dream.
text ...Fuko rests her head on my shoulder.
text @[Tomoya]
text Fuko...?
text Not a word from her.
text Instead, the gentle breathing sounds answer to me.
text Her sleeping face is flickering in the firelight.
text I'm gazing upon but a fleeting dream.
